---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
    title="Front End Developer for Agencies | Day Rate Contractor"
    description="Freelance front end developer with 18+ years' experience, ready to slot into your agency team. Astro, WordPress, Sanity, design systems. Day rate available.">
    <section class="section">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="grid grid--compact">
                <div class="grid-item grid-item--10">
                    <h1 class="mb-1">Front End Development Support for Agencies</h1>
                </div>
                <div class="grid-item grid-item--8">
                    <p class="text-lg">
                        Extra capacity when you need it, without the overhead of hiring. I work as an embedded contractor alongside agency teams - picking up
                        sprints, covering gaps, or owning a build end-to-end under your brand.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--padded bg-blue-dark color-white mb-0">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="grid grid--compact">
                <div class="grid-item grid-item--10">
                    <h2 class="mb-1">Why agencies bring me in</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="grid-item grid-item--8">
                    <ul class="flow">
                        <li>
                            <strong>Fast to onboard.</strong> I've worked inside agencies for years - ready to adapt to your processes and workflows.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>White-label ready.</strong> I work under NDAs as an extension of your team. Clients see your agency, not a subcontractor.
                        </li>
                        <li><strong>Flexible engagement.</strong> Day rate, project-based, or ongoing retainer - short sprints or multi-month builds.</li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Senior-level output, no supervision needed.</strong> I can take design assets to a shipped, accessible, performant build with
                            minimal oversight.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="grid grid--compact">
                <div class="grid-item grid-item--10">
                    <h2 class="mb-1">What I cover</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="grid-item grid-item--8">
                    <ul class="flow">
                        <li>
                            <strong>Front end build</strong> HTML, CSS, JavaScript, TypeScript, component-driven builds, responsive & accessible by default.
                        </li>

                        <li><strong>Frameworks & static site generators</strong> Astro, 11ty, React, Next.js.</li>

                        <li><strong>Backend & CMS integration</strong> PHP, WordPress, Sanity, Storyblok</li>

                        <li>
                            <strong>Design systems</strong> Storybook, Fractal, component libraries built from Figma.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <strong>QA & audits</strong> Technical SEO, accessibility (WCAG) and performance audits - useful for pre-launch sign-off or cleaning up
                            an existing build.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section id="get-in-touch" class="section section--padded bg-blue-dark color-white mb-0">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="grid">
                <div class="grid-item grid-item--8 flow">
                    <h2 class="h1">Availability</h2>
                    <p>
                        Need help with your website or an extra pair of hands on your next project? Currently taking on new agency partnerships from Sept 2026.
                        Get in touch to check current availablity.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <a href="/contact" class="button button--secondary">Get in touch</a>
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>
